\label{lem-Kahane}
Let $\nu$ be a finite Borel measure  on $[0,1]$. If $\nu$  is supported on  a sub-interval $I\subset [0,1]$ of length $|I|<1$,  then its Fourier dimension is given by 
\begin{align}\label{Fdim-lattice}
\dim_F(\nu)= \sup\Big\{D \in [0, 1]: \text{$| \widehat{\nu}(n)| \le c_D (1+ |n|)^{-  D /2}$ for all $n \in  \mathbb{Z}$} \Big\}.
\end{align}

For any $p>1$, the  $L^p$-dimension of $\nu$ is defined by
\begin{align}\label{def-D-p}
\underline{\dim}_p(\nu): = \liminf_{n\to\infty} \frac{-\log \big(\sum_{|u|=n}  \nu(I_u)^p\big) }{ n  (p-1)\log b}.
\end{align}

